  "term": "succinylcholine",
  "definition": "Succinylcholine is a short-acting muscle relaxant that works by activating nicotinic receptors at the neuromuscular junction and causing depolarization. Because this effect can persist, it disrupts nerve-to-muscle signaling and is followed by skeletal muscle relaxation and flaccid paralysis.",
